@ [canonical_uuid] 591865d2-2253-451c-81e1-8bd6b5b81d03

& [Need]
  + pinned Git documentation proves the future worktree-add checkout can invoke post-checkout
  + unbound hooks attributes fsmonitor maintenance lazy fetch optional locks and protocol behavior would make a physical receipt under-explain its effects
  + leaving these surfaces latent before implementing a runner would convert ambient machine state into undeclared authority

& [SmallestCorrection]
  + retain the exact twelve children and one mutating worktree-add operation
  + add one uniform six-pair Git prefix and three closed environment entries
  + add one empty hook directory one empty attribute file and exact carrier and info-attributes gate facts
  + revise only forms and tests whose meaning or effect counts change

& [WhyNotBroader]
  + production runner commission authentication physical locking concurrent-hostile mutation and a retained attempt require separate authority and evidence
  + provider model MCP Phase3A P1 SWA-06B writer and activation are unrelated to closing Git materialization helpers
  + current storage fails the unchanged physical floor

& [Decision]
  + Revision 0.4 is necessary bounded and non-widening
